# Where threads may be created (ADR 0003). Both files are future homes: the named-thread helper
# in lector-base (ADR 0005) and the scheduler's own workers. Nothing else may call
# thread::spawn / thread::Builder / spawn_scoped, so every current use is baselined.
crates/lector-base/src/thread.rs
crates/lector-app/src/scheduler.rs

# Closed list of owner-thread kinds for lector_base::thread::spawn_named (ADR 0003, decision 3):
# a thread that is itself a long-lived resource. Provisional spellings until spawn_named exists;
# comparison ignores case, `-` and `_`. Adding a kind needs an ADR.
kind:pty-reader
kind:pty-writer
kind:lsp-reader
kind:askpass-listener
kind:file-watcher
kind:scheduler-worker
